Figure 4, a confocal microscopy image, demonstrates the enhanced uptake of antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) when formulated with Nano-11 nanoparticles. The top row shows efficient internalization of AF647-labeled Nano-11 (red) by BMDCs. The middle row indicates very limited uptake of soluble FITC-labeled ovalbumin (OVA) (green) when presented alone. However, the bottom row clearly shows that when OVA is adsorbed to Nano-11, both Nano-11 (red) and OVA (green) are efficiently co-localized and phagocytized by the BMDCs. This visual evidence supports Nano-11's role in significantly improving antigen delivery to dendritic cells, a crucial mechanism for its adjuvant effect.